Below is a line‑by‑line assessment of the current source, followed by a set of concrete recommendations that address the most common OWASP Top 10 risks (injection, broken authentication/authorization, missing validation, etc.).  
Even though the current code is tiny and does not accept user‑supplied data, it is a good opportunity to harden the **foundation** so that future features can be added safely.

