## 📋 Recommendations & Code Samples

Below is a **step‑by‑step** hardening plan. Implement the changes in order; each block can be added to the existing file or split into separate modules (which is the recommended pattern for larger projects).

### 1️⃣ Split app definition & server start (better testability & configuration)

**app.js** – define the Express app *only*.

```js
// app.js
require('dotenv').config();                // Load .env (never commit .env!)
const express = require('express');
const helmet = require('helmet');
const cors   = require('cors');
const morgan = require('morgan');
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');

const app = express();

// ---------- Security Middlewares ----------
app.use(helmet());                          // Sets many secure headers
app.use(cors({                               // Restrict origins in prod
  origin: process.env.CORS_ORIGIN || '*',   // Change '*' to your front‑end domain
  methods: ['GET','POST','PUT','DELETE'],
}));
app.use(morgan('combined'));                // Access logs (A09)
app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' }));   // Body size limit

// Rate limiting – stop simple DoS / brute‑force
const limiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 min
  max: 100,                // limit each IP to 100 reqs/window
  standardHeaders: true,
  legacyHeaders: false,
});
app.use(limiter);

// ---------- Routes ----------
app.get('/health', (req, res) => {
  res.json({ status: 'ok', timestamp: new Date().toISOString() });
});

/* Protected /users route – see section 2 for auth */
app.use('/users', require('./routes/users'));

module.exports = app;
```

**server.js** – the actual listener (helps with unit‑testing).

```js
// server.js
const app = require('./app');

const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;
app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`🚀 Server listening on ${PORT}`);
});
```

> **Why?**  
> *Separating the app from the server allows test frameworks to import the Express instance without starting a listening socket.* It also lets you inject different environment variables per environment (dev, test, prod).

