### 3.7  Protect Against SSRF (A10) – Future Guidance

Whenever you fetch a URL provided by a client (e.g., webhooks, image proxy), **whitelist** the allowed hostnames or IP ranges and enforce a DNS‑resolution timeout.

```js
function isAllowedUrl(url) {
  const allowedHosts = ['api.trusted.com', 'assets.example.com'];
  try {
    const { hostname } = new URL(url);
    return allowedHosts.includes(hostname);
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
}
```

