| **Error Logging** | Use a structured logger (e.g., `pino`, `winston`) and ship logs to a SIEM. | Verify errors are written to log file/stdout without stack traces in production responses. |
| **Dependency Management** | Pin versions in `package.json`; run `npm audit` CI step. | CI should fail on any known CVE. |
| **HTTPS Everywhere** | Deploy behind a TLS-terminating reverse proxy (NGINX, Traefik) or enable Node HTTPS in dev. | `curl -I https://...` should show `Strict‑Transport‑Security` header. |
| **Security Testing** | Add automated scans: OWASP ZAP, npm `audit`, `npm run test:security`. | CI pipeline should block new vulnerabilities. |
| **Environment Secrets** | Store `API_KEY`, DB passwords, etc., in `.env` or secret manager; never commit to Git. | `.gitignore` contains `.env`; repo history has no secrets. |

