### 1️⃣ Keep `.env` files *out* of the production image

| Action | Command |
|--------|---------|
| Add .env and any other env files to `.gitignore` (if you ever create them) | ```bash<br>echo ".env*<br>.env.test" >> .gitignore<br>git add .gitignore<br>git commit -m "Ignore env files"</br>``` |
| Ensure the test canary file stays **committed** (it is useful for detection), but rename it to something clearly non‑production, e.g., `canary.env`. | ```bash<br>git mv .env.test canary.env<br>``` |

